      "body": "## What\n\n`test_kandinsky6_bf16_dtype.py::test_attention_backend_dispatch_and_repeated_forward[*-FA]` (added in #42743) fails on the scheduled AMD run (`multimodal-gen-test-1-gpu-amd`). Test-only fix, no runtime changes.\n\nFailing run: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38563492873/job/115850314797\n\n## Why\n\nOn ROCm the FA backend resolves to Torch SDPA (FA3 is CUDA-only, and `flash_attn` is not in the image), so the \"must not silently fall back\" assert fails. The test already skips FA on SM12.x for the same reason; this adds the same skip for ROCm.\n\nThis PR originally also fixed `test_server_args.py::test_fasth3_selects_vsa_h3_for_the_transformer` on ROCm. Main has since fixed that upstream (the shared CUDA mock now pins `is_rocm`), so the merge with main takes main's version of that file.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- MI300: the FA cases skip and the TORCH_SDPA cases pass ([job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38755083928/job/116491534135)).\n- CUDA: the multimodal unit suite passes ([job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38820876644/job/116731184729)).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39262941748](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262941748)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39262941729](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262941729)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39262941758](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262941758)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "stayinalive181"
            },
            "body": "Some MI355X data in support of keeping `aiter` as FastH3's transformer default on ROCm. Setup: `lmsysorg/sglang-rocm:v0.5.21-rocm10-mi35x-20261014`, 1× MI355X.\n\n- **The kernel itself works on gfx950.** The in-tree VSA-H3 Triton forward passes `test_vsa_h3_attention.py` (12 passed).\n- **It is slower than dense aiter at 10% block density.**\n\n  | Tokens (24 heads, head 128) | VSA-H3 Triton | Dense aiter |\n  | --- | ---: | ---: |\n  | 64k | 69.4 ms | 42.5 ms |\n  | 32k | 17.6 ms | 10.6 ms |\n\n  The VSA-H3 numbers use `num_stages=2, waves_per_eu=2, matrix_instr_nonkdim=16`. The pinned Hopper/Blackwell launch (`num_warps=4, num_stages=5`) is slower still, at 91.3 ms for 64k.\n- **End to end it would need more work.** Routing `video_sparse_attn_h3` on ROCm stops in `flash_attention_v3.flash_attn_varlen_func` with `No module named 'flash_attn'`.\n- **The aiter default works.** FastH3 V2 t2va at 1344×768, 5 s, 8 steps takes 34.8 s on one MI355X.\n\nSo the CUDA-only VSA-H3 default looks like the right call for ROCm today.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-15T17:12:29Z",
            "databaseId": 6197884956,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-15T17:12:29Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44421#issuecomment-6197884956"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "michaelzhang-ai"
            },
            "body": "Thanks for the data. To be clear on scope, this PR is test-only and doesn't change backend selection: FastH3 still defaults to VSA-H3 only on CUDA, and ROCm keeps its `aiter` default. The new `test_fasth3_keeps_the_rocm_default_backend` case pins that, so routing ROCm to VSA-H3 later would mean updating that test on purpose. @stayinalive181 \r\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-15T17:58:04Z",
            "databaseId": 6198752830,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-18T22:26:33Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44421#issuecomment-6198752830"
          },
