    "body": "## What\n\n`test_kandinsky6_bf16_dtype.py::test_attention_backend_dispatch_and_repeated_forward[*-FA]` (added in #42743) fails on the scheduled AMD run (`multimodal-gen-test-1-gpu-amd`). Test-only fix, no runtime changes.\n\nFailing run: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38563492873/job/115850314797\n\n## Why\n\nOn ROCm the FA backend resolves to Torch SDPA (FA3 is CUDA-only, and `flash_attn` is not in the image), so the \"must not silently fall back\" assert fails. The test already skips FA on SM12.x for the same reason; this adds the same skip for ROCm.\n\nThis PR originally also fixed `test_server_args.py::test_fasth3_selects_vsa_h3_for_the_transformer` on ROCm. Main has since fixed that upstream (the shared CUDA mock now pins `is_rocm`), so the merge with main takes main's version of that file.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- MI300: the FA cases skip and the TORCH_SDPA cases pass ([job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38755083928/job/116491534135)).\n- CUDA: the multimodal unit suite passes ([job](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38820876644/job/116731184729)).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39262941748](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262941748)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39262941729](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262941729)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39262941758](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262941758)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
